When subagents are available, fan out read-only discovery scouts and one
reviewer per analysis dimension (see the rubric owned by the analysis
prompt); otherwise run the same checks sequentially. Agent-managed
sub-agents dispatch the plan's `## Work Units` / `## Parallel Plan` /
execution Subplans at execution time — Ralph-managed worker fan-out is
dormant in the bundled default.

Choose the executor-facing shape by delegation size:

- `## Work Units` contains small bounded tasks or verification gates. Keep
  every executable step, including a final integration gate, inside a declared
  unit.
- A substantial execution-subagent mini-plan belongs under a repeatable
  `## <Name> Subplan` or `## Subplan: <Name>` heading.
- A large multi-surface plan normally fans out four or five independent
  execution Subplans, then uses an ordinary `## Integration and Verification`
  section for main-session integration and verification.

Agent-managed sub-agents return implementation and proof to the main
execution session; Ralph-managed worker fan-out is dormant in the bundled
default. If the user's request targets Ralph Workflow's own planning
internals and is not a concrete bug report with a reproduction, plan against
`ralph/...` paths in this repository; otherwise plan against the user's
project.

