## Plan artifact contract

The complete grammar, severity model, and `## Validation Overrides` ledger
live in `.agent/artifact-formats/plan.md`.

Submit one native-markdown document:

1. Use `type: plan` frontmatter. Write context as prose and structured values
   as labeled fields. The hard anchors are `type: plan`, unique `### [S-n]`
   steps, and resolvable consumed references. An exact, case-sensitive
   `## Work Units` or `## Parallel Plan` heading opts into fail-closed
   unit-marker parsing; use arbitrary headings for descriptive prose.
2. Write each step as a complete `### [S-n] Title` block (for example
   `### [S-1] Title`) with description prose and fields such as `Type:`,
   `Files:`, `Depends on:`, and `Verify:`. IDs are stable and never
   renumbered. Recommended built-in `Type:` values
   are `file_change`, `action`, `research`, and `verify`; project-specific
   `Type:` values are accepted and preserved verbatim. Pair every `Verify:`
   with a specific `Expect:` result or name a specific `Evidence:` /
   `Location:` artifact.
3. Validate with {{VERIFY_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}
   (`artifact_type="plan"`, `content` = the document), then repair every
   line/section/rule diagnostic. Override any advisory finding by recording
   a reason under `## Validation Overrides`; errors cannot be overridden.
4. Submit with {{SUBMIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} (same arguments).
5. To revise a plan, edit it in place with {{EDIT_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}
   (`artifact_type="plan"`, `edits` = a list of `oldText`/`newText` pairs).
   That call submits the plan as soon as the edited draft validates, so no
   separate {{FINALIZE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} call is needed; inspect
   the draft with {{GET_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} when you need its current
   text. Every submission stages its document as the draft, so this works
   after a rejected submit. Resend the whole document via
   {{STAGE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} (`mode="replace_all"`) only for a
   wholesale rewrite.
6. For a long plan, use {{STAGE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}},
   {{GET_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_REFERENCE}}, and {{FINALIZE_MD_ARTIFACT_TOOL_REFERENCE}};
   {{DISCARD_MD_DRAFT_TOOL_REFERENCE}} intentionally restarts the draft.
7. A valid artifact receipt—or a validated, promoted fallback receipt—is
   mandatory. After that receipt exists, you MUST call
   {{ DECLARE_COMPLETE_TOOL_REFERENCE }} as the final explicit action.